# Cursor rules for sunheart-ai

You are contributing to Sunheart AI — open-source treasury intelligence.

## Read first
1. README.md
2. AGENTS.md (the AI contract — every time)
3. MATHEMATICS.md (the 8 kernel layers)
4. ISSUES.md (the 5 good-first-issues)

## House rules
- Pure functions in `kernel/`. No I/O, no chain calls, no globals.
- Update `tests/` for every `kernel/` change.
- Anchor every change to a kernel layer (cite the number in the PR body).
- No new dependencies in `kernel/` without justification.
- Python 3.10+ stdlib only inside `kernel/`. Extras live in `adapters/`.

## Verification
- `python -m unittest discover tests -v` must pass
- `python examples/first_contribution.py` must produce ranked output
- CI runs on Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12

## Voice
Caveman clarity in commits and PR bodies. Point first, evidence after. No marketing voice.
